<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/img/favicon.svg"><link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="96x96" href="/favicon.png"><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/img/favicon.svg"><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="theme-color" content="#8B0000"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"><title>Raft/Mat Foundation Design in Edinburgh</title><meta name="description" content="Expert raft/mat foundation design in Edinburgh. Geotechnical analysis for soft soils, variable groundwater, and"><link rel="canonical" href="https://edinburgh.geotechnical-engineering.biz/raft-mat-foundation-design/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:title" content="Raft/Mat Foundation Design in Edinburgh"><meta property="og:description" content="Expert raft/mat foundation design in Edinburgh. Geotechnical analysis for soft soils, variable groundwater, and"><meta property="og:url" content="https://edinburgh.geotechnical-engineering.biz/raft-mat-foundation-design/"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Edinburgh Uk"><meta property="og:image" content="https://edinburgh-uk.geotechnical-engineering.biz/img/losa-de-cimentacion-4.webp"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_UK"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:title" content="Raft/Mat Foundation Design in Edinburgh"><meta name="twitter:description" content="Expert raft/mat foundation design in Edinburgh. Geotechnical analysis for soft soils, variable groundwater, and urban constraints. BS EN 1997 & Eurocode 7..."> <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","itemListElement":[{"item":"/","@type":"ListItem","name":"Home","position":1},{"@type":"ListItem","name":"Raft/Mat Foundation Design in Edinburgh","position":2}],"@type":"BreadcrumbList"}</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","description":"Expert raft/mat foundation design in Edinburgh. Geotechnical analysis for soft soils, variable groundwater, and urban constraints. BS EN 1997 & Eurocode 7 compliant.","name":"Raft/Mat Foundation Design in Edinburgh","provider":{"@type":"LocalBusiness","name":"Edinburgh Uk","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressCountry":"UK","addressLocality":"Edinburgh"},"email":"contact@geotechnical-engineering.biz","telephone":""},"areaServed":{"@type":"City","name":"Edinburgh"},"url":"https://edinburgh-uk.geotechnical-engineering.biz/losa-de-cimentacion","@type":"Service"}</script>
<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"When is a raft foundation better than strip footings in Edinburgh?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A raft is preferable when the allowable bearing capacity of the surface soil is low (below 80 kPa) or when the building loads are high enough that individual footings would overlap. In Edinburgh's soft clays and made ground, a raft distributes loads evenly and reduces differential settlement risks."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the typical cost range for raft/mat foundation design in Edinburgh?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The cost for a full geotechnical investigation and structural design of a raft foundation for a typical residential project in Edinburgh ranges from £890 to £3,670, depending on site size, number of boreholes, and complexity of the ground conditions."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does groundwater affect raft foundation performance?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"High groundwater reduces the effective stress in the soil, decreasing bearing capacity and increasing the risk of buoyancy uplift. In Edinburgh, where the water table can rise to 2 metres in winter, raft designs must include permanent drainage or a thickened slab to resist hydrostatic pressure."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a raft foundation be used on sloping sites in Edinburgh?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, but the design must account for lateral earth pressure and potential sliding. A stepped raft with reinforced concrete ribs or a combined raft-and-retaining-wall system is common on Edinburgh's hillsides. A slope stability analysis is always required before finalising the geometry."}}],"@type":"FAQPage"}</script>
